---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Container from "../../components/shell/Container.astro";
import Section from "../../components/content/Section.astro";
import ContentDocument from "../../components/content/ContentDocument.astro";
import { getStaticOgImagePath } from "../../lib/og-image";
import { withAutoOgImage } from "../../lib/seo";

const seo = withAutoOgImage(
  {
    title: "Colophon · Webxsid",
    description: "Notes on how this site is built and maintained.",
    canonical: "/colophon",
  },
  getStaticOgImagePath(),
);
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Colophon · Webxsid"
  description="Notes on how this site is built and maintained."
  seo={seo}
  backHref="/"
>
  <Container>
    <div class="py-8 lg:py-14">
      <div class="max-w-4xl space-y-14 lg:space-y-16">
        <Section title="Colophon">
          <div class="space-y-7">
            <p class="ui-lead max-w-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-text">
              A small record of how this site is put together, revised, and kept
              in use.
            </p>
            <ContentDocument class="mt-2">
              <h2>Why this site exists</h2>

              <p>
                Most portfolio sites eventually become snapshots. They capture a
                moment in time, then slowly drift out of sync with the work they
                were meant to represent.
              </p>

              <p>
                This site is an attempt to avoid that. Rather than treating it
                as a finished artifact, I treat it as a working document.
                Projects evolve, ideas change, old assumptions get replaced, and
                the site changes alongside them.
              </p>

              <p>
                The goal is not completeness. The goal is to maintain a place
                where the work, the reasoning behind it, and the things that
                influence it can live together.
              </p>

              <h2>How it is built</h2>

              <p>
                The site is built with Astro and styled with Tailwind CSS.
                Content is stored as Markdown and rendered through Astro Content
                Collections.
              </p>

              <p>
                Pages are intentionally simple. There is no CMS, very little
                client-side JavaScript, and no attempt to optimise for
                engagement. Most of the site is static HTML generated at build
                time.
              </p>

              <p>The structure mirrors the way I think about my work:</p>

              <ul>
                <li>Projects for systems and tools.</li>
                <li>Writing for essays, observations, and technical thinking.</li>
                <li>
                  References for books, articles, songs, and ideas that stayed
                  with me.
                </li>
                <li>
                  Work for the teams and systems that shaped my approach to
                  engineering.
                </li>
                <li>Now for whatever currently has my attention.</li>
              </ul>

              <h2>Design</h2>

              <p>The visual design is intentionally restrained.</p>

              <p>
                Over time I've found myself preferring software that becomes
                clearer the closer you get to it. The same idea applies here.
                Typography, spacing, and structure carry most of the interface.
                The goal is to make reading feel effortless rather than
                decorative.
              </p>

              <p>
                Many modern portfolios feel like products. I wanted this site to
                feel more like a notebook.
              </p>

              <h2>Maintenance</h2>

              <p>
                The site is maintained intermittently, usually alongside
                whatever project or idea I'm currently exploring.
              </p>

              <p>
                Most updates are small: a note added, a page rewritten, a
                project updated, a thought recorded before it disappears.
              </p>

              <p>
                There is no roadmap. Only whatever seems worth documenting next.
              </p>
            </ContentDocument>
          </div>
        </Section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Container>
</BaseLayout>
